WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.202
Welcome to Module 10, Reshaping Data in PostgreSQL.

00:00:04.202 --> 00:00:08.522
Reshaping changes structure, not the underlying facts.

00:00:08.522 --> 00:00:15.957
We will move between long and wide forms, pivot categories into columns, unpivot columns back into rows,

00:00:15.957 --> 00:00:20.972
preserve meaningful NULL values, and protect the intended analytical grain.

00:00:20.972 --> 00:00:27.377
The most important habit in this module is to say what one output row represents before you write

00:00:27.377 --> 00:00:33.777
the reshape query. Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:33.777 --> 00:00:38.362
a BI dashboard turning monthly categories into presentation columns.

00:00:38.362 --> 00:00:45.302
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:45.302 --> 00:00:48.937
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:48.937 --> 00:00:53.157
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to

00:00:53.157 --> 00:00:59.242
defend later: what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:59.242 --> 00:01:03.520
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
